:4a9f66a88daac80ad6e5b3e92d3350bd9a9da15dca2931a8d278eff62725d05c","file":"preprints/A-counterexample-to-Tachikawas-second-conjecture-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":23,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"0c4a1e42446954e504bb76f9928aa5cce14d168e6e7b4b940f75c64dace8a8c4","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/A-counterexample-to-Tachikawas-second-conjecture-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:4a9f66a88daac80ad6e5b3e92d3350bd9a9da15dca2931a8d278eff62725d05c","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/A-counterexample-to-Tachikawas-second-conjecture-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L23"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nLet\n\\[\n k=\\mathbb F_2(q,H_1,H_2),\n\\]\nwhere $q,H_1,H_2$ are algebraically independent.\nThere exist a finite-dimensional associative unital symmetric\n$k$-algebra $A$ and a finite-dimensional unital left $A$-module $M$\nsuch that $M$ is nonprojective and\n\\[\n \\Ext_A^i(M,M)=0\\qquad\\text{for every integer }i>0.\n\\]\nIn particular, Tachikawa's second conjecture is false."}
